Z||000003||Raydar||10-26-2000||10:36 PM||||AA has a mixture (I'm led to believe) of refurbed and new radios. I tried really hard to buy a radio from them, and finally gave up. I was trying to buy the UP3 (I think) Grand Am CD player. The guy (James?) said that he had one refurbed one in stock, but if I could wait for a couple of days he was getting "many" skids of new radios in. Said he'd check for a new UP3. To make a long story short, I called back 4-5 times, over a period of 2-3 weeks. Each time, I was put off for another couple of days, or the guy was "in a meeting", or some other silliness. Was supposed to return my calls. Never did.<BR> Well, Screw that!<BR>Finally went and bought the Pioneer 1.5 DIN.<BR>If you want a Delco radio, try <A HREF="http://www.newellelectronics.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.newellelectronics.com/</A> <BR>Several folks on the Forum have used them, and seem to be very pleased.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-26-2000).]||||reg||9
